Z||000007||Cozmo||05-28-2001||09:05 AM||||Put 100+ miles down yesterday, myself and 3 other Fieroites driving. The general consensus is <B>wow</B>. Had the accelerator cable fall off and the starter solenoid stuck on once <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> but besides that she runs GREAT!!!<BR>Gonna go thru the brakes and fix some electrical gremlins today and then she's ready for an interior and paint.<BR>   I painted the engine two-tone gold and argent hammer finish. Very tough stuff, it disguises surface imperfections really good and is holding up to the temps fine so far.<BR>   Yeah, SSFiero, I gor disgusted and thought about selling it a while back...BOY AM I GLAD I DIDN'T!!! That was IDIOTIC.<BR>   I'm thinking of doing the interior tan and painting it British racing green.  Just got a compressor, It'll be my first paint job!<BR><B>C02M0</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||6
Z||000008||trigger||05-28-2001||09:22 PM||||Can you latch the top back on?  Does it leak?  How do you store the top?  Looks really good. Is it an auto or a stick?<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Trigger.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Cozmo||05-29-2001||09:20 AM||||Yeah Trigger, the top does latch on. Yes it does leak real bad, but the rubber weatherstrip is all torn up.  It should seal pretty good when I go thru and replace it.  The only place to store the top (besides the garage) is to bungee cord it to the luggage rack (boy does it look STUPID there).  Maybe I'll get some BIG stanchions and mount it like a wing <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> (Uncle Ben racing).<BR>Seriously, I'm thinking of making a snap-on canvas top just in case it rains when the hardtop is in the garage.<BR>  The car is a 4 speed with a subframe, very similar to some convertibles I've seen.<BR>BTW, put over 250 miles on it this weekend..<BR>It's a <B>BLAST!</B><BR><B>C02M0</B>||||reg||1
